1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,419
<i>A sorry letter?</i>

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:03,336
<i>For Billy?</i>

3
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,588
<i>Oh, it's a song.</i>

4
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:07,674
<i>- Did you forget something?</i>
<i>- Here.</i>

5
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:11,594
<i>I have millions of followers</i>
<i>across all social media platforms.</i>

6
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,430
<i>I can ask them to repost it.</i>

7
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,390
<i>Why are you doing this?</i>

8
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>Because I still…</i>

9
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,520
<i>Let's wait for Mommy.</i>

10
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:26,317
[ENRICO] <i>Dear, please hear me out.</i>

11
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,028
[BILLY] <i>That's not necessary.</i>

12
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:31,322
<i>Let this be the last time</i>
<i>we see each other.</i>

13
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:34,159
<i>We were doing fine,</i>
<i>weren't we, Auntie Pres?</i>

14
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:35,452
<i>We were doing just fine.</i>

15
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,370
<i>He's ruining everything.</i>

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:39,456
<i>We were doing fine.</i>

17
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:41,166
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

18
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,292
[KNOCKING]

19
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:44,085
Yes, Auntie?

20
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:51,176
Are you going to file a case?

21
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:56,765
Yes, Auntie.

22
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,060
If he won't stay away from me
and my brother.

23
00:01:01,811 --> 00:01:04,898
Termination of Parental Authority

24
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,984
on the grounds of neglect and abandonment.

25
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,780
Is that for me?

26
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:14,991
It's for the sanctuary.
I got it.

27
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:18,870
And you don't have to come in tomorrow.
I know you have a lot on your mind.

28
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:21,081
- Don't worry about it.
- No, it's all right, Auntie.

29
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:22,165
It's okay.

30
00:01:22,248 --> 00:01:26,085
I have a responsibility to the sanctuary.

31
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:27,170
I can do this.

32
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:30,131
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

33
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:36,971
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:17,846
I still think about my husband.
[SNIFFLES]

35
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:19,180
Even though…

36
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,976
Even though he cheated on me…
[SNIFFLES]

37
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:24,060
…and left me,

38
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:27,230
I still want to get back together.

39
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:31,151
For our child's sake.

40
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,280
I'm pregnant.

41
00:02:35,363 --> 00:02:37,615
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

42
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:38,867
<i>Mommy, you're pregnant?!</i>

43
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,410
[CHUCKLES]

44
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,162
[GASPS, EXCLAIMS]

45
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,789
<i>We'll be having two kids to take care of.</i>

46
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:47,083
<i>Please don't leave us anymore.</i>

47
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:52,797
<i>Just stay here, Dad.</i>
<i>Don't work on the ship anymore.</i>

48
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:55,091
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>
- [BOTH CHUCKLE, GIGGLE]

49
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,426
[YOUNG BILLY SQUEALS]

50
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,346
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>Please don't leave us, Dad!</i>

51
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,724
[CRYING] <i>Please.</i>

52
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,058
[YOUNG BILLY]<i> Mommy, please--</i>

53
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:07,228
<i>Don't waste your tears on worthless men.</i>

54
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:11,357
[SOBS] I don't want
my child to be fatherless.

55
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,819
My child deserves a complete family.

56
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:18,781
I understand you, Gelica.

57
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:23,745
There is nothing wrong with wanting
a complete family for your child.

58
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:28,249
However, don't rush into
making a decision.

59
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,252
Especially after
everything you've been through.

60
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:35,340
But it is difficult to raise
a child on your own.

61
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,593
Maybe you can still work it out.

62
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:41,888
Give your husband another chance.

63
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,015
Gelica?

64
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:48,728
If you're willing
to give him another chance,

65
00:03:49,854 --> 00:03:51,731
he should earn it.

66
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:56,110
Not through words or promises,

67
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:57,570
but through action.

68
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:01,950
He should show that he'll be responsible

69
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,703
and make things right.

70
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:09,958
If he ever does it again,

71
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:12,210
if he ever leaves you again,

72
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:15,755
it will hurt a lot more.

73
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,341
And it will hurt your child too.

74
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:22,679
What matters most right now
is you and your baby.

75
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:25,139
We are all here to support you.

76
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:28,810
We want the best for you.

77
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:35,608
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:44,450
You had a lot of jobs
in Canada, Mr. Dominguez.

79
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:49,622
How come you never
stayed at one job for long?

80
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:53,251
Um, to be honest, ma'am,

81
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:55,086
I was undocumented.

82
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,587
Oh…

83
00:04:56,671 --> 00:05:00,967
But I stayed because I had to
provide for my family back here.

84
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,469
Why did you come back?

85
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,972
My children are all grown up.
They can support themselves now.

86
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:09,684
And I also want to spend time with them,

87
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:14,272
and to keep working,
so I'm not a burden to them.

88
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,483
Actually, ma'am,

89
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:21,279
I have a lot of experience
as a canteen supervisor

90
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:24,449
at Maplewood University in Canada.

91
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:26,451
Ah…

92
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:30,705
Out of all the applicants,
you are the most qualified.

93
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:32,498
But…

94
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:36,210
we won't be able to match
your salary in Canada.

95
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:39,172
Don't expect too much,
Mr. Dominguez. [CHUCKLES]

96
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:40,923
Money is not an issue for me.

97
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:43,051
I just want a job.

98
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:46,345
I can start now, ma'am.

99
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:50,266
I can keep track of
the inventory and sales.

100
00:05:50,349 --> 00:05:52,852
Could I take a look at the menu?

101
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:54,937
I can see how we can improve it

102
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,274
while keeping it within the guidelines
and the kids' budget.

103
00:05:58,357 --> 00:06:00,985
Wow, okay.

104
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:04,030
You can start today, Mr. Dominguez.

105
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:05,448
Thank you. Thank you, ma'am.

106
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:07,825
I'll need your police clearance,
all right?

107
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:10,203
Ah, ma'am…

108
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,330
Can I submit that later?

109
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:14,123
Oh, okay. No problem.

110
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:16,584
- Thank you.
- [CHUCKLES] Thank you.

111
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:24,759
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:34,936
I am so proud of you, my dear.

113
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:38,272
I know you're going through
a lot with your dad,

114
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:41,150
but you didn't give in to
your emotions earlier.

115
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,237
Your advice will be a big help for Gelica.

116
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,198
I just don't want anyone to experience

117
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:51,452
what Oliver and I went through.

118
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:54,831
Not all fathers are like ours. Right?

119
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:58,042
Hopefully, her husband has changed,

120
00:06:58,126 --> 00:07:00,128
so their family can still be together.

121
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:02,588
I know you're still hurting.

122
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:06,551
Can you still do this?

123
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,094
I can.

124
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:13,224
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:21,816
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

126
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:23,276
What happened?

127
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:28,072
My mother's not doing well.

128
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,993
Sometimes, she's quiet.

129
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:34,745
Unresponsive.

130
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:37,623
Then she will get violent all of a sudden.

131
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:39,167
That explains my bruise.

132
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:43,045
Abi, maybe she needs professional help?

133
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:48,759
You mean a mental facility?

134
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,428
It wouldn't be possible.

135
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,346
I don't have a budget for that.

136
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:56,184
My internet cafe
isn't making enough money.

137
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:59,854
We can assess your mom here.
We could do that for you.

138
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:02,690
Then we can refer her
to mental health facilities

139
00:08:02,773 --> 00:08:05,860
or community-based services.

140
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:08,279
Ms. Precious, I know my mother.

141
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:11,532
She'll refuse
any kind of assessment or test.

142
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:14,702
What I need is another source of income.

143
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:17,622
My internet cafe isn't making money.

144
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,373
It's going bankrupt.

145
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,876
Ms. Billy, maybe…?

146
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:27,006
Sorry, Abi, but there's
no vacancy at LoveList.

147
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:33,721
Uh, what about here at Angels of Grace?

148
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:38,851
I have a degree in marketing.

149
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:40,061
Uh…

150
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:43,773
I know about
computer hardware and software.

151
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:47,276
I'm the one who fixes the computers
in my shop when needed.

152
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:51,364
But our volunteers here
only receive an allowance.

153
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:54,450
It's not even enough to cover
their transportation and food.

154
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,330
Don't worry, Abi.

155
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:04,043
If there's an opening at LoveList,
you'll be the first to know.

156
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:07,880
- Really, Ms. Billy?
- Mm-hmm.

157
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,131
Thank you.

158
00:09:09,215 --> 00:09:10,633
Mm-hmm.

159
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:15,012
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:16,806
[TONI] Based on our estimate,

161
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:21,185
the initial investment allocation
for this new feature

162
00:09:21,269 --> 00:09:25,106
allows us to scale
without affecting our cash flow.

163
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:28,776
Bills? Are you still with us?

164
00:09:28,859 --> 00:09:30,736
Yes! Yes! Of course I am.

165
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,906
Um, Charm, do you have
the competitor analysis?

166
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:38,995
For today, I suggest we zero in on this.

167
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,873
Pebblng has received
a lot of positive reception

168
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:47,295
because of their newly-launched
Heart Reward Scheme.

169
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:49,422
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:09:49,505 --> 00:09:53,384
So every successful match
gets a free dinner

171
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:54,927
at their partner restaurants.

172
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:56,137
Exactly.

173
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:59,473
So the free dinner incentive works
even though

174
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:03,853
there's no way to verify
if those are actual successful matches?

175
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:04,812
[CHARM] Yes, chief.

176
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:09,525
Those successful matches
could just be friends

177
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:13,738
who pretended to match for a free dinner.

178
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:17,199
- So it's easy to fake it.
- Right.

179
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:20,161
[BILLY] But attention is currency.

180
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:22,246
The data will show if it worked.

181
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,457
So, what's your plan, Billy?

182
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:26,751
Why do you seem quite calm?

183
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,338
[BILLY] Okay.

184
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,547
Okay.

185
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:36,260
Actually, when I heard about
the Heart Reward Scheme,

186
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:37,928
I knew it would be trouble.

187
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,098
So I did my homework.

188
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:45,645
I researched, and I went back
to our previous FGDs.

189
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:47,730
And one thing kept coming up.

190
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:51,484
People don't just want matches.

191
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:54,320
They want something real.

192
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,238
But how?

193
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:57,239
A wedding?

194
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,660
If we are the real deal,

195
00:11:00,743 --> 00:11:03,663
we won't just be with them
until the first date.

196
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:07,166
We'll be with them until the wedding.

197
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:09,251
They give them free dinners.

198
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:11,212
We give them a wedding package.

199
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:13,214
- [CLAPS]
- Awesome!

200
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,590
I love it!

201
00:11:14,673 --> 00:11:17,051
[VALERIE] Because it's like
we're giving a statement too.

202
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:19,178
Because, you know,
you can't just fake a wedding.

203
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:21,472
- Yes.
- Which proves that…

204
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:23,432
LoveList is the real deal.

205
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:27,228
So for those who meet through LoveList
and decide to get married,

206
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:28,354
we'll pay for it.

207
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:32,733
- So lit, chief. I'm so in!
- How cool!

208
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,235
- That's brilliant!
- [TONI] But!

209
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:36,070
That's expensive.

210
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,530
Not if we do it right.

211
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:40,116
We bring in sponsors, caterers,

212
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:42,034
wedding gown designers,
and everything else!

213
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:43,285
[VALERIE] I can cover that.

214
00:11:43,369 --> 00:11:47,748
There's actually a lot of deals coming my
way. People are begging for a collab.

215
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,209
So, yeah. I'll make the calls.

216
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:52,211
Okay! Thank you, Val.

217
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:54,755
[VALERIE] Yeah. And Toni!

218
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:57,133
This is going to be good for you and Yani,

219
00:11:57,216 --> 00:12:00,219
because isn't he a struggling painter?

220
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,096
I mean, I don't mean to offend you,

221
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:05,474
but for sure, you'll have
a tight budget for your reception.

222
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:08,686
You might only
serve <i>pancit</i> then. [GIGGLES]

223
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:10,896
But I mean, you don't have to worry

224
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,731
because this is all for free now.

225
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:14,942
So, it's perfect, right? [VALERIE GIGGLES]

226
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:17,111
[FORCED LAUGH] Perfect!

227
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,195
- [VALERIE GIGGLING]
- Val…

228
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:22,324
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:26,036
Charm, please include this for our meeting
with Ms. Lindsay on Friday.

230
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,496
Okay.

231
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,123
But…

232
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:31,083
what should we call this?

233
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:38,674
So, LoveList has LoveLine and LoveSpeak.

234
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:41,343
Now, it also has…

235
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:44,763
LoveFeast.

236
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:47,016
What do you guys think?

237
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:49,518
- Good! LoveFeast!
- LoveFeast!

238
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,061
- LoveFeast!
- LoveFeast!

239
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:53,522
- LoveFeast is good, yes?
- [CHEERING]

240
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:57,067
- [SQUEALING, WHOOPING]
- LoveFeast!

241
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:00,112
You know what, Suzie?

242
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,573
I'm learning how to box now.

243
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:04,950
Wow! Just like Manny Pacquiao?

244
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:06,994
Isn't that painful?

245
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,746
That's what the gloves are for.

246
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:13,125
Ah, so you're learning that
to be prepared for Biboy?

247
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:15,211
So I can protect you.

248
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:16,670
Really?

249
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:18,339
Aww.

250
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:19,340
Okay, let me teach you.

251
00:13:19,423 --> 00:13:21,258
First, here's a straight punch.

252
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:23,302
That's a straight punch.
And then, this is a hook.

253
00:13:23,385 --> 00:13:25,471
[SUZIE] Ah, I know that one. Boom!

254
00:13:25,554 --> 00:13:26,680
[CHUCKLING]

255
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,682
What are you doing? You do boxing now?

256
00:13:29,558 --> 00:13:31,560
Do you really think you can handle me now?

257
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:32,811
Do you really want to know?

258
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,439
Would you like to be suspended again?

259
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:38,150
Boy, he's acting tough!

260
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,318
You've got some nerve, huh?!

261
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,111
That's enough!

262
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,782
I saw what you did.

263
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:46,325
Would you like me to report you?

264
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:47,868
- Go away.
- Sorry, sir!

265
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,495
- Sorry! Sorry!
- Let's go!

266
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:56,418
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:08,430
Thank you, sir.

268
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,015
Oh, by the way, I'm--

269
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:13,727
I'm Eric. I was recently hired
as a canteen supervisor.

270
00:14:14,728 --> 00:14:16,814
- And you, what's your name?
- I'm Oliver.

271
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:19,733
Oliver? Oh, Oliver!

272
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:21,527
Oliver.

273
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,612
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:26,031
And she's my friend, Suzie.

275
00:14:26,115 --> 00:14:27,324
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

276
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:31,328
If someone tries
to mess with you here again,

277
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:33,747
you know where to find me, okay?

278
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:35,666
I'll be here in the canteen.

279
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:37,543
Thank you again, Sir Eric.

280
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,044
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you very much.

281
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,589
- All right.
- Let's go, Suzie.

282
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:45,175
[GENTLE MUSIC FADING]

283
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,678
[VALERIE] Billy!

284
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,805
Oh, yes, Val?

285
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:53,225
So, I called Floramour already
for the flower arrangements

286
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:56,312
because they've been nagging me
for how many months already,

287
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,772
and they're so glad
that I called them back.

288
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:01,609
But yes, anyways, good news.

289
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:05,112
They're very excited to be
a part of the LoveFeast project.

290
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:08,824
Wow! That's really good news.

291
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:11,035
Val, thank you.

292
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,245
No.

293
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,663
Thank you.

294
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:18,500
Because after all the dramas
and what I did to you,

295
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:20,502
you really covered for me.

296
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,130
Everyone else doubted me, but not you.

297
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:25,549
It's really nice
to have someone believe in me.

298
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:27,343
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

299
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:30,137
I think we should really be besties!

300
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,475
- Yeah? [GIGGLES]
- [BILLY CHUCKLES FAINTLY]

301
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:39,730
Have some coffee first.

302
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,315
You look too serious.

303
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:43,150
Yes. Thank you.

304
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,111
[BILLY] Are you busy?

305
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,238
Not really.

306
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:51,241
Oh, dude. I spoke to
Attorney Elle about the case.

307
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:52,159
Mm-hmm.

308
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:56,038
She managed to get her hands
on the police records of Caloy Toledo.

309
00:15:56,121 --> 00:15:58,499
[JORDAN] He used to be
the leader of a street gang.

310
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:02,544
Involved in robbery,
harassment, extortion…

311
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,338
Honestly, I'm not surprised.

312
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:08,133
He was even implicated in a fight
that resulted in a casualty.

313
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:10,636
But no one pursued the case.

314
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:11,637
Wow.

315
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,723
When are you meeting Caloy again?

316
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:16,433
Next week.

317
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:19,228
The subpoena has already been issued.

318
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:23,691
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:26,110
Sir Jordan, excuse me.

320
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:28,529
The server traffic has tripled.

321
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:31,115
The login rate and match requests
are too high!

322
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:32,533
Okay, that's fine.

323
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:35,744
We may need auto-scaling

324
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:38,914
or temporary load balancing
to avoid crashing the site.

325
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:40,541
I'll check it in a bit.

326
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,251
Okay, sir.

327
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:46,505
The system is flooding!
It's a good problem to have.

328
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:49,216
- Is that so?
- Congrats, dude.

329
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:51,468
- Are you still handling things well?
- Yes.

330
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,262
You're dealing with your bar,

331
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:54,680
with Grandpa Jude,

332
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:56,265
with Caloy's case,

333
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:57,850
and now, this.

334
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:01,687
I mean, can we afford to hire
one more person for the tech team?

335
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:05,441
[VEHICLES HONKING]

336
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,819
[CALOY] Abi!

337
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,322
What?

338
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:15,284
What's that?

339
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:19,038
[PAPER RUSTLES]

340
00:17:24,918 --> 00:17:27,046
- Ouch!
- I told you so!

341
00:17:27,129 --> 00:17:29,256
See? You had him locked up.
He won't leave you alone.

342
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:30,841
I wouldn't be surprised

343
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:33,552
if they found out
more information about you.

344
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:35,387
- You are so stubborn!
- [SCOFFS]

345
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:37,222
They can dig all they want.

346
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,265
Hey!

347
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:39,892
They won't find anything on us.

348
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:43,145
What will they find on me?
On you? Nothing!

349
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,440
And that driver won't say anything.

350
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:50,110
Don't worry about it.
I'll take care of it.

351
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:52,362
You better make sure of that.

352
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:54,615
That hurt, you know. Can I get a kiss?

353
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:56,742
- Come on.
- You want a kiss?

354
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:58,035
- Nice try!
- Ow!

355
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,536
- That hurt.
- [PHONE RINGS]

356
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,829
Cut it out.

357
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:03,082
Look.

358
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,833
[RINGING CONTINUES]

359
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:10,130
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:11,423
[ABI CLEARS THROAT]

361
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:15,385
Hello, Ms. Billy Idol?

362
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:21,850
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

363
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,727
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

364
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:26,105
You have a university degree?

365
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,856
Yes, Ms. Billy.

366
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:32,569
I graduated in 2014. Cum laude.
[CHUCKLES]

367
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:37,950
It says here

368
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:43,455
that your first internship
and your first job was at PhilComm Press.

369
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,458
Tell me about your experience.

370
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:50,379
That was a great experience
for me, Ms. Billy.

371
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:53,841
PhilComm Press is one of
the top three media companies in Asia.

372
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:56,260
I was one of the five interns
from our batch.

373
00:18:56,343 --> 00:19:00,222
After my internship,
they eventually hired me.

374
00:19:00,305 --> 00:19:01,431
Abi.

375
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:04,852
Most of your experience is in marketing.

376
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:09,439
How did you develop an interest in IT?

377
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:12,442
[CHUCKLES] Sir Handsome,
my father was into tech.

378
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:15,988
He had a gadget repair shop.

379
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:19,199
That's how I got into tech as well.

380
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:23,745
I don't have formal training.
I'm self-taught.

381
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:24,955
Okay.

382
00:19:25,038 --> 00:19:28,667
Since you have your own internet cafe,

383
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:32,254
you must know a lot about data privacy.

384
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:34,173
So the question is,

385
00:19:35,465 --> 00:19:38,719
how would you protect
our users' personal data,

386
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:43,140
like private messages, profiles, etc.?

387
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:44,766
Encryption is key.

388
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,769
Use HTTPS to protect data in transit

389
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:51,648
and encrypt your database
to protect data at rest.

390
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:54,318
Strong authentication, restricted access,

391
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:56,528
so your system doesn't get hacked.

392
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:59,364
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

393
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:00,866
Piece of cake.

394
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:04,203
Okay, let's move on to the performance.

395
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,205
- Mm-hmm.
- Let's say…

396
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:09,708
the matchmaking feature slows down…

397
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,001
Mm-hmm.

398
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:12,753
…during peak traffic hours.

399
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:14,046
What would you do?

400
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,339
Check the server first.

401
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:19,176
Or you can go straight to
enabling auto-scaling

402
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:20,928
so it can keep up with the traffic spike.

403
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,347
Ah, I would check the server first.

404
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:26,308
Or we can go straight to
enabling auto-scaling

405
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,518
so it can keep up with the traffic spike.

406
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:31,104
That's right.

407
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:37,027
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

408
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:41,448
Okay, so I think we can
wrap up this meeting.

409
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,659
We'll review your application.

410
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:45,744
Thank you so much for your time, Abi.

411
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:48,872
Thank you, Ms. Billy Idol.
Thank you. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

412
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:51,166
Sir Handsome, thank you, thank you.

413
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,709
- Thanks, Abi.
- I really hope I get it.

414
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,211
I want to be a part of LoveList.

415
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,630
Please, Ms. Billy. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

416
00:20:56,713 --> 00:20:58,131
Thanks again.

417
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:02,427
I'll wait for your call, Ms. Billy.

418
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:04,554
- Mm-hmm.
- Thank you again, idol.

419
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,223
Sir Handsome, thank you.

420
00:21:06,306 --> 00:21:09,726
[INTRIGUING MUSIC SWELLS]

421
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:17,859
Jordan and I were impressed with her.

422
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,321
Well, there's nothing wrong with

423
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:25,575
verifying the information
on her resume, right?

424
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:30,038
Sorry for giving you more work.

425
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,750
Why did you ask me to check this?

426
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,627
Human Resources could've done this.

427
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:37,963
Because I know you
had a bad feeling about her.

428
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:40,716
And now is your chance…

429
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:45,137
To prove I'm onto something.

430
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:46,888
To be honest, Charm,

431
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:51,435
I find her odd too.

432
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:53,562
At first, it was okay.

433
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:56,356
You know, it was flattering.

434
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:58,775
But after a while…

435
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:00,861
It started getting weird?

436
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:06,575
There you go.
So why let her apply for a job?

437
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:10,078
You feel sorry for her.

438
00:22:10,787 --> 00:22:11,997
Hmm?

439
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,625
I want to help her.

440
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:16,543
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

441
00:22:16,626 --> 00:22:20,589
But, you know,
there's really something about her.

442
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:24,176
Then I guess let's see.

443
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:29,639
Let's see if she deserves
to be given a chance.

444
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:33,643
Okay.

445
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:41,777
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

446
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:51,870
<i>- I'll introduce you to Sir Eric.</i>
- [BILLY] <i>Okay.</i>

447
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:54,790
<i>Oliver just wanted</i>
<i>to give something to Sir Eric.</i>

448
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:56,124
[JORDAN] <i>I want him</i>
<i>to go to jail.</i>

449
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:58,168
<i>For what he did to my friend.</i>

450
00:22:58,251 --> 00:23:00,337
<i>- I was just following orders!</i>
<i>- Who gave you those orders?</i>

451
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:02,839
<i>Sorry I can't be there with you.</i>

452
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,382
<i>Don't worry about me.</i>

453
00:23:04,466 --> 00:23:05,842
<i>I got this.</i>

454
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:07,469
<i>Good luck.</i>

455
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:09,971
[ABI] <i>I'm going to be part of</i>
<i>the LoveList family.</i>

456
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,307
<i>I'm reviewing Abi's resume.</i>
<i>She's lying to us!</i>

457
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,308
[ALARM RINGS]

458
00:23:13,391 --> 00:23:16,144
<i>Don't panic! Let's exit</i>
<i>calmly, okay?</i>

459
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,772
[ALARM BLARING]
